{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xJ57Jbs3nktquWEBiz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gin's recovery middleware no longer treats `http.ErrAbortHandler` as a crash. That value is the standard way to deliberately abort a handler, and `net/http` doesn't log it either. Gin now handles it the same way it handles a broken connection: it logs one line, records the error on the context and aborts, with no stack trace and no 500 sent.\n\n- **`recovery.go`:** I added the `errors.Is(err, http.ErrAbortHandler)` check, which also matches wrapped versions of the error.\n- **`recovery_test.go`:** the new `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` checks that the status already set by the handler is kept and that no \"panic recovered\" stack is logged. The recovery and panic tests pass, and gofmt is clean.\n\nThe middleware recovers the panic instead of re-panicking. So `net/http` never sees it and won't drop the connection the way it would without Gin in front. Nothing is committed yet, and you're on a detached HEAD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":34360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":671,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc5a0650-68c7-4148-ac08-744d7d102bca","uuid":"f0cfac58-5161-4b25-9efb-4df2ff0d5fbe","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:39:49.901Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xJ4sAeeGR3m9mcg28f"}
